# Third-round probes replayed against the final tree (this commit)
#
# Every finder probe of workflow wf_67cbe503-425 run unchanged against the fixed provenance/recovery.py and
# egregore/goals.py. Last 22 lines of each, cut at 260 columns.
#
# Reading the results:
#  - fix-apply p1_kill_matrix: 54 SIGKILL points, openable-and-unrecorded=0, exactly-one-correct-event=54/54.
#  - stale or foreign plans: never resumed (resumed=False; the new tear is quarantined as itself).
#  - lost newline (event + NUL), short writes, read-back failures: resumed or RecoveryInterrupted then completed.
#  - stops: torn autonomy.regressed, business.terminated, repair.provider_withdrawn, omnimorph.organ_retired, a
#    supersede, a kill capsule: refused until stop_record (or warned when cut before the deciding field); a
#    supersede torn in its second append leaves the old goal superseded (executor calls on it: 0).
#  - over-refusal probes: ordinary records accepted without stop_record.
#  - template probes: refused, except a payload bit flip with no hash digit visible (the documented residual) and
#    partial_unverified / content_complete_unverified cases, which demand complete_record.
#  - power-loss mixes reported 'NOT RECOGNIZED' are states in which none of the plan's distinguishing bytes
#    reached the disk: the retry quarantines the bytes as they stand and reports the first quarantine as
#    unrecorded (deliberate; see the deliberation record's counterevidence).
#  - the two EXIT 1 runs (fix-space/p8b, adv-protocol/p3) call recovery with no acknowledgments expecting a stale
#    plan to be resumed; it is not, so the fresh tear needs 'unanchored' and is refused.

